--TEST--
`Fiber`, `Thread`, `Worker` and `parallel\Runtime` are not declared, PHP's concurrency functions are not functions that exist, and a generator has none of the coroutine methods — `rule:concurrency/one-scheduler`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:concurrency/what-does-not-exist
var $fiber = new Fiber(fn(): int => 1);
var $thread = new Thread();
var $worker = new Worker();
var $runtime = new parallel\Runtime();

// The same refusal reaches a type position: none of these is a name a program may write.
class Holder {
    public function park(Thread $t): Worker {
        return $t;
    }
}

// `Core\Task::map` is what `curl_multi_*` was for, and it is a member rather than a
// free function, so the old names resolve to nothing at all.
var $pid = pcntl_fork();
var $multi = curl_multi_init();
var $run = parallel(fn(): int => 1);

// A generator answers an `Iterator<T>`, which is walked and never driven: there is no
// `send`, no `throw` and no `getReturn` to resume it with.
class Steps {
    public static function upTo(int $n): Iterator<int> {
        yield $n;
    }
}

var $steps = Steps::upTo(3);
$steps->send(1);
$steps->getReturn();
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0303]: `Fiber` is not declared
%A
error: aborting due to 11 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
